      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The original has significant understandability issues:\n1. Lots of dead code (unused fields, methods, and imports from the parent test class)\n2. The loop uses a countdown (`i > 0; i--`) instead of a cleaner ascending form\n3. Unnecessary comment duplication with obvious codeThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused dead code (unused imports, fields, and helper methods inherited from the original parent test class) and replaces the non-obvious countdown loop with a clearer ascending `for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)` form, while preserving identical runtime behavior."
